msgid "MatrixMap puts interactive maps on your site without an API key or account. It makes three kinds of map: <strong>maps</strong> with your places, shapes and routes; <strong>store locators</strong> that find the nearest of your locations; and <strong>region maps</strong> — the world, a country or its regions, coloured with your data."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:197
msgid "Install and activate"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:199
msgid "In WordPress go to <strong>Plugins → Add New</strong>, search for “MatrixMap” and click <strong>Install Now</strong>, then <strong>Activate</strong>. Or upload the plugin zip under <strong>Plugins → Add New → Upload Plugin</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:200
msgid "A <strong>MatrixMap</strong> menu appears in the admin sidebar, with the Dashboard, Maps, Locations, Analytics, Settings, Import & Tools and these Docs."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:201
msgid "Requirements: WordPress 6.5 or newer and PHP 7.4 or newer."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:203
msgid "Your first map in three minutes"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:205
msgid "Go to <strong>MatrixMap → Add New Map</strong>. Give the map a name (only you and screen readers see it) and pick a starting point: one location, places with a list, a store locator, countries you serve, a data map, a route — or a blank map."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:206
msgid "Click <strong>Create map</strong>. The editor opens with the settings on the left and a live preview on the right. The button in the top bar switches full screen on and off."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:207
msgid "Add places: type an address and click <strong>Search</strong>, or click <strong>Add place</strong> and then click the map. Click a place in the list to edit its title, popup text, picture, phone and button link."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:208
msgid "Click <strong>Publish</strong> (or <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>/<kbd>⌘</kbd>+<kbd>S</kbd>)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:209
msgid "Show it on a page: click <strong>Create page</strong> in the top bar (also in the Maps list) to get a draft page with the map on it, add the <strong>MatrixMap</strong> block to an existing page and choose the map, or paste the shortcode shown in the top bar (for example <code>[matrixmap id=\"12\"]</code>). Elementor has a MatrixMap widget."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:211
msgid "Recommended setup"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:213
msgid "<strong>Map look:</strong> Settings → Maps & style. Vector maps (the default) need no key and are free for any traffic. Set your brand colour so buttons, markers and highlights match your site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:214
msgid "<strong>Privacy:</strong> Settings → Privacy & consent. If you use a consent plugin, maps wait for consent by default; you can also make every map “click to load”. Region maps contact no outside service at all."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:215
msgid "<strong>Many addresses?</strong> Settings → Address search. The free OpenStreetMap search allows about one lookup per second; for large imports choose a service with a key."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:216
msgid "<strong>Store locator:</strong> add your locations under MatrixMap → Locations (or import a spreadsheet) before building the locator."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:218
msgid "Where things are"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:219
msgid "Screen"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:219
msgid "What it is for"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:220
#: src/Admin/Menu.php:45
#: src/Admin/UI.php:174
msgid "Dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:220
msgid "Stats, a setup checklist, templates, recent maps and a health check."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:221
msgid "All maps, with their type, content and shortcode. Row actions: Edit, Duplicate, Export."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:222
msgid "The places your store locator and maps can use: address, coordinates, hours, contact details, categories."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:223
#: src/Admin/Menu.php:51
#: src/Admin/Menu.php:64
#: src/Admin/UI.php:177
msgid "Analytics"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:223
msgid "Store locator searches and clicks (with MatrixMap Pro)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:224
msgid "Site-wide defaults: map look, providers and keys, address search, visitor location, privacy, performance."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:225
#: src/Admin/Menu.php:53
#: src/Admin/Tools.php:204
#: src/Admin/UI.php:179
msgid "Import & Tools"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:225
msgid "Import locations, export data and maps, switch from another map plugin, maintenance."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:238
msgid "Build a store locator from a spreadsheet"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:240
msgid "Download the sample CSV from <strong>Import & Tools → Import locations</strong> and fill it in (name, address, city, postcode, country; latitude/longitude if you have them; phone, email, website, category, hours)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:241
msgid "Upload it, check how each column is matched, and start the import. Rows without coordinates are looked up by address; very large files take a while with the free OpenStreetMap search (about one address per second)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:242
msgid "Go to <strong>Add New Map</strong> → <strong>Store locator</strong>. Choose which categories it searches, the radius choices, whether the search radius is drawn on the map as a circle (on for new locators; maps made before keep their look until you turn it on), and what happens when the page opens."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:243
msgid "Publish and add it to a page with the Store Locator block or its shortcode. Optionally add a <strong>Store Search</strong> box on your home page that sends visitors to the locator."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:245
msgid "Make a data map (colour countries or states by value)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:247
msgid "Add New Map → <strong>Data map</strong>. Pick the map (world, a country, its regions, US counties or a detailed map)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:248
msgid "Under <strong>Regions</strong>, open “Import from a spreadsheet” and paste two columns: region name or code, and value. Names like “USA”, “Ivory Coast” or “Los Angeles County” are recognised."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:249
msgid "Under <strong>Style</strong>, “Colour by value” is on: choose the palette, the scale and the number of steps; give the legend a title."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:250
msgid "Optional: region names on the map, a search box or list of regions, and what a click does (open a link, or show the region’s details beside the map or in a pop-up)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:252
msgid "Switch from another map plugin"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:254
msgid "Go to <strong>Import & Tools → Switch from another plugin</strong>. MatrixMap lists the maps it found from WP Go Maps, MapPress, WP Maps, Interactive Geo Maps (MapGeo), Maps Marker Pro / Leaflet Maps Marker and others."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:255
msgid "Click <strong>Import</strong>. The other plugin’s data is only read, never changed; importing again updates the same maps instead of making copies."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:256
msgid "Deactivate the old plugin. Its shortcodes and blocks on your pages now show the MatrixMap version, so you don’t have to edit pages."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:258
msgid "Copy maps to another site"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:259
msgid "Export the maps under <strong>Import & Tools → Export</strong> (or use the Export link on a map in the Maps list) and import the file on the other site. Imported maps arrive as drafts. Pictures from the Media Library are not included; locations are exported separately as CSV or GeoJSON."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:260
msgid "Load maps only after consent"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:261
msgid "Settings → Privacy & consent. With a supported consent plugin active (WP Consent API, Complianz, Cookiebot, CookieYes, Borlabs or iubenda), maps that load tiles from another server wait for consent and show a short placeholder. You can also make every map “click to load”. Region maps never need consent because they use no outside service."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:262
msgid "Add a map in a page builder"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:263
msgid "Gutenberg: the MatrixMap, Store Locator, Region Map and Store Search blocks. Elementor: the MatrixMap widget. Any builder: the shortcode from the map’s top bar. MatrixMap Pro adds elements for Bricks, Divi and WPBakery."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:264
#: src/Admin/Docs.php:704
msgid "With MatrixMap Pro"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:266
msgid "<strong>Directions on the map:</strong> Settings → Directions, choose a routing service. Locator results get a “Route” button and map popups “Directions on the map”."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:267
msgid "<strong>Dealer network:</strong> add the “Submit a location” block set to “Dealer sign-up”, review applications under Locations → Pending, then add the “Dealer enquiry” block so customers reach their nearest dealer."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:268
msgid "<strong>Posts on a map:</strong> in a map’s Places tab turn on “Posts on this map”, then put the “Posts map (Query Loop)” block inside a Query Loop."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:269
msgid "<strong>Region data from a Google Sheet:</strong> in a region map’s Regions tab, paste the sheet link under “Data from a Google Sheet or feed”."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:271
msgid "These guides need MatrixMap Pro."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:283
msgid "A map shows your places, shapes and map files on a street, satellite or styled map. Find it under <strong>MatrixMap → Maps</strong>; the editor has tabs on the left (Places, Shapes, Style, Settings, Import) and a live preview with desktop, tablet and phone views."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:284
msgid "Places and popups"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:286
msgid "Add a place by address, by coordinates (e.g. <code>48.858, 2.294</code>) or by clicking the map; drag a marker to fine-tune it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:287
msgid "Each place has a title, popup text (bold, italic, links, lists), a picture, a phone number, a button link, and a marker style (pin, dot, picture or icon; colour and size)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:288
msgid "<strong>Categories</strong> group places; visitors can filter them with category filter buttons."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:289
msgid "Settings → <strong>List and filters</strong> adds a list of places beside or below the map — it also helps keyboard and screen reader users — with an optional search box and category filter buttons. <strong>Clustering</strong> groups nearby places when there are many."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:290
msgid "<strong>Category legend</strong> (Settings → List and filters): a small key over the map with each category’s colour and name, in the corner you choose."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:291
msgid "<strong>Popup layout</strong> (Settings → Popups): <em>Card</em> puts the picture on top, <em>Side by side</em> puts it beside the text, and <em>Compact</em> shows only the title, opening status, address and buttons."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:292
msgid "Places from <strong>Locations</strong> can be added to any map (Settings → Locations library)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:294
msgid "Editor shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:296
msgid "<strong>Ctrl/⌘ + Z</strong> undoes the last change and <strong>Ctrl/⌘ + Shift + Z</strong> (or Ctrl + Y) redoes it — also the arrows in the preview bar. Inside a text field the browser’s own text undo applies."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:297
msgid "<strong>Ctrl/⌘ + S</strong> saves the map (Update or Publish). <strong>Esc</strong> stops “Add place” mode."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:299
msgid "Shapes and map files"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:300
msgid "The Shapes tab draws areas, lines and circles, each with its own colour and popup. You can also add a GPX, KML or GeoJSON file (for example a hiking track or delivery zones) from the Media Library or a web address."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:301
msgid "Map engine and look"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:302
msgid "Engine"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:302
