msgid "The familiar Google look."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:305
msgid "Yes (Google API key)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:307
msgid "If a visitor’s browser can’t run vector maps (WebGL switched off or unsupported), the map is shown with image tiles instead of staying blank."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:308
msgid "Size, view and behaviour"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:309
msgid "Settings sets the height (and a separate height on phones), the starting view (“Use this view” in the preview bar stores what you see), the zoom limits, which controls show, how scrolling zooms the map, what popups open on, and whether the map waits for consent."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:310
msgid "Pro adds: posts of any post type on the map (from latitude/longitude fields, an ACF map field or an address), a road route drawn through the places with distance and time, elevation profiles for GPX tracks, heatmaps and a 3D globe view."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:322
msgid "A store locator lets visitors find your nearest locations by address, postcode or their own position, and shows the results on a map and in a list with distance, opening status, directions and a call button."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:324
msgid "Locations are kept once and used everywhere: <strong>MatrixMap → Locations</strong>. Each has an address (found on the map with <strong>Find on map</strong>), phone, email, website, opening hours with holidays and a “closed until” date, extra details (for example parking or languages), categories, a description and a featured image."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:325
msgid "Locator settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:327
msgid "<strong>Which locations:</strong> all, or only some categories."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:328
msgid "<strong>Radius choices</strong> and the default radius; distances in km or miles (Settings → Maps & style)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:329
msgid "<strong>When the page opens:</strong> show all locations, or wait for a search; optionally start near the visitor’s approximate location (no permission prompt) when your host provides it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:330
msgid "<strong>Suggestions</strong> as visitors type: matching store names, cities and postcodes from your own locations."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:331
msgid "<strong>Filters</strong> from your extra details (for example “Parking”), <strong>countries</strong> to limit address search to, and the most results to show."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:332
msgid "<strong>Layout:</strong> results beside the map (left or right), below it, or as a grid."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:333
msgid "<strong>Sort</strong> (off by default): visitors can order the results by distance, name or “open now first”. <strong>Copy link</strong> (off by default): a button after a search that copies a link opening the same search."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:334
msgid "<strong>Shareable links:</strong> a search updates the page address, so <code>?mm_near=Berlin&amp;mm_r=25</code> (or the short <code>?near=Berlin</code>) opens the locator with that search; <code>?mm_lat=…&amp;mm_lng=…</code> uses an exact point and <code>?mm_locate=1</code> asks for the visitor’s position."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:335
msgid "<strong>Very large libraries:</strong> above 50,000 published locations, maps and locators that show every location load the visible area as the map moves (Site Health tells you when this applies)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:337
msgid "Store Search box"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:338
msgid "The Store Search block (or <code>[matrixmap_search page=\"ID\"]</code>) is a small search box for your header or home page. It sends visitors to the locator page with their search, or with “Use my location”."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:339
msgid "Pro adds: an “Open now” filter, in-map directions with turn-by-turn steps, result templates (cards, photos, compact), anonymous search and click analytics with a “demand where you have no store” map, SEO pages for every location with LocalBusiness data, messages to locations, WooCommerce “Where to buy”, location submissions, dealer sign-up and enquiries routed to the nearest dealer."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:351
msgid "Region maps show the world, a continent, a country or its regions as clickable shapes. They are drawn by your site itself, so they contact no outside service and need no consent."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:352
msgid "The map library"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:354
msgid "The world (countries or continents), US states and the counties of every US state."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:355
msgid "The states, provinces or regions of more than 200 countries."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:356
msgid "Detailed maps: French departments, Italian and Spanish provinces, UK local authorities, German districts, Indian districts, Australian council areas, New Zealand districts, Canadian economic regions, Philippine provinces and the municipalities of each Mexican state."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:358
msgid "Type in the map picker to search the list."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:359
msgid "Adding data to regions"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:361
msgid "Click a region on the preview (or in the list) to give it a value, a colour, a name to show, details, a group and a link — or to hide it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:362
msgid "Tick several regions to colour them, set a value or a link at once."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:363
msgid "Paste from a spreadsheet: region names or codes and values."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:365
msgid "Style options"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:367
msgid "<strong>Colour by value</strong> with 10 palettes (two are colour-blind safe), equal ranges, quantiles or a smooth gradient, and a legend whose ranges can be clicked to highlight regions. Or show values as <strong>bubbles</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:368
msgid "<strong>When a region is clicked:</strong> open its link, or show its details below the map or in a pop-up."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:369
msgid "<strong>Find a region:</strong> a search box or a list beside the map; a region selected when the page opens; links can pick one with <code>?mm_region=CODE</code>."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:370
msgid "<strong>Starting view:</strong> zoom in on chosen regions (e.g. only Europe on the world map) and limit how far visitors can zoom."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:371
msgid "<strong>Tooltips</strong> on hover, on click or off; region names on the map; <strong>regions without data</strong> shown, faded or hidden (the map then frames the rest)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:372
msgid "<strong>Markers</strong> on region maps as dots, pins or your own icons, with names, and lines between them."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:373
msgid "A “Show data as a table” link gives screen reader users the same information."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:375
msgid "Pro adds: click actions that open a picture gallery, a video, one of your pages or another web page; drill down from the world into countries, states and counties; combined maps (the world with states and provinces); your own maps from SVG or GeoJSON (floor plans, sales territories); and region data from categories, posts with a region field, a Google Sheet or a JSON feed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:387
#: src/Admin/Tools.php:131
msgid "Import locations"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:388
msgid "Import & Tools → Import locations takes a CSV file (UTF-8, comma or semicolon separated). You match each column to a field, choose whether rows update existing locations (same reference ID, or same name and address), and follow the progress. A sample file shows the expected columns."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:389
#: src/Admin/MapEditor.php:516
#: src/Admin/Tools.php:132
#: assets/src/admin/builder/panels/Data.js:229
#: build/admin/builder.js:2
#: build/builder-modal.js:3
msgid "Export"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:391
msgid "<strong>Locations</strong> as CSV (for spreadsheets) or GeoJSON (for other map tools)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:392
msgid "<strong>Maps</strong> as a MatrixMap file, to copy them to another site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:393
msgid "<strong>Settings</strong> as a file (API keys are left out), to copy them from staging to live."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:395
#: src/Admin/Tools.php:155
msgid "Switch from another plugin"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:396
msgid "Maps from WP Go Maps, MapPress, WP Maps (WP Google Map Plugin), Interactive Geo Maps / MapGeo, Maps Marker Pro / Leaflet Maps Marker (layers and markers become maps; <code>[mapsmarker]</code> keeps working) and others can be imported. Maps kept inside pages (Leaflet Map shortcodes, WP Map Block) can be shown by MatrixMap once the original plugin is deactivated."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:397
#: src/Admin/Tools.php:156
#: src/Admin/Tools.php:345
msgid "Maintenance"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:398
msgid "Rebuild the location index if the locator misses locations after a direct database import; clear the address search cache if an address moved."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:399
msgid "Pro adds scheduled data sync from Google Sheets, CSV or JSON: stable IDs, change detection, a preview, a log and email alerts, and a safety check that stops a run from unpublishing most of your locations. Sources may be up to 25 MB and 20,000 rows, served as CSV or JSON (a web page is refused); every download is pinned to the address that passed MatrixMap’s private-network check, redirects included."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:400
msgid "Private Google Sheets (Pro)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:401
msgid "Sheets that must stay private are read by a Google service account instead of a public link:"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:403
msgid "In Google Cloud, create or open a project and enable the <strong>Google Sheets API</strong> and the <strong>Google Drive API</strong> (APIs & Services → Library)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:404
msgid "Under IAM & Admin → Service accounts, create a service account, open its Keys tab and add a <strong>JSON</strong> key. Paste the downloaded file’s contents under Settings → Data sync. The key is stored encrypted, never shown again and never exported."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:405
msgid "In Google Sheets, share each sheet with the service account’s email address (Viewer is enough). “Test the service account” lists the spreadsheets it can read."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:406
msgid "Under Import & Tools → Data sync, add the sheet’s normal link and choose <strong>Private sheet</strong> as the access. A tab other than the first is chosen with its #gid=… in the link."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:408
msgid "Staging to live"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:410
msgid "On staging, export the maps you changed (Export → Maps) and, if needed, your settings (Export → Settings)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:411
msgid "On the live site, import the settings file, then the maps file. Maps arrive as drafts, so you can check them before publishing. API keys are never in these files: each site keeps its own."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:412
msgid "Locations move as CSV or GeoJSON (Export → Locations, then Import locations on the other site). Rows with the same reference ID update the existing location instead of adding a copy."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:414
msgid "With Pro, the same moves can be scripted with WP-CLI (<code>wp matrixmap maps export</code>, <code>wp matrixmap settings import</code>…) — see Developers → WP-CLI."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:425
msgid "MatrixMap Pro is active on this site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:425
msgid "MatrixMap Pro is a separate plugin that adds these features to the same screens. Your maps keep working if a Pro license lapses; the license brings updates and support."
msgstr ""

