#: src/Admin/Docs.php:502
msgid "Turn on <strong>Settings → Advanced → Allow maps to be embedded on other websites</strong>. Each published map’s editor bar then has a <strong>Copy embed code</strong> button (the <code>&lt;iframe&gt;</code> code); the frame loads <code>/?matrixmap_embed=ID</code>, a page with nothing but the map (marked “noindex”). Only published maps are served; while the setting is off the address answers 404."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:503
msgid "Sample data"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:504
msgid "New site? <strong>Dashboard → Add sample data</strong> creates ten locations in three categories, a store locator, a map with places and a data map, so you can see every kind of map at once. <strong>Remove sample data</strong> deletes exactly those again (a category you started using for your own locations is kept)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:505
msgid "Pro shortcodes: <code>[matrixmap_nearest]</code>, <code>[matrixmap_geo]</code>, <code>[matrixmap_posts]</code>, <code>[matrixmap_where_to_buy]</code>, <code>[matrixmap_submit]</code>, <code>[matrixmap_my_locations]</code>, <code>[matrixmap_lead]</code>, <code>[matrixmap_static id=\"12\"]</code> (a PNG of a map), <code>[matrixmap_compare left=\"12\" right=\"13\"]</code> (two maps with a slider), plus the Nearest location, Geo content, Submit a location, Dealer enquiry, Compare maps and Posts map (Query Loop) blocks."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:517
msgid "MatrixMap works inside the page builders and form plugins you already use. Everything here is a map or field you pick from a list — no shortcodes to type."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:518
msgid "Elementor"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:519
msgid "The <strong>MatrixMap</strong> widget (category “MatrixMap”) shows any saved map — a map, a store locator or a region map — with a live preview in the editor. Choose the map and, if you like, a height."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:520
msgid "Pro adds a <strong>MatrixMap location</strong> group of dynamic tags for single location templates (Theme Builder → Single Post → Locations): Location name, Address, Street, City, Postcode, Country, Coordinates, Phone, Email, Opening hours, Open now, Directions link, Website link, Call link, Location page link, Photo and Map image. Each tag reads the current location, or one you pick. The “Map” tag feeds the widget’s map picker, so a template can choose its map dynamically. The Map image tag needs a Google, MapTiler or Mapbox key under Settings → Providers & API keys."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:521
msgid "Bricks, Divi, WPBakery and Oxygen"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:522
msgid "Pro adds a MatrixMap element to Bricks, Divi (4 and 5), WPBakery and Oxygen: pick a map, set a height. Oxygen: “+ Add” → Other → MatrixMap."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:523
msgid "JetEngine"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:524
msgid "In a JetEngine listing of locations, the Dynamic Field widget has a <strong>MatrixMap location</strong> source with a field picker (address, hours, open now, directions link, map image…). The same fields appear as a “MatrixMap location” group in every Post/Object data select, so they work in Dynamic Link, Dynamic Image and conditions too."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:525
msgid "Meta Box"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:526
msgid "A <strong>MatrixMap location</strong> field type (<code>matrixmap_location</code>): an address with latitude and longitude. Leave the coordinates empty and the address is found on the map when the post is saved. The value is stored as <code>lat,lng</code>, like Meta Box’s own map and OSM fields, so any of them puts posts on a map: map editor → Posts on this map → Position from → “A Meta Box map, OSM or MatrixMap location field”."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:528
msgid "Locations from forms"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:529
msgid "A WPForms, Fluent Forms or Gravity Forms form can create a location from each entry. In the form builder, map the form fields to the location’s name, street, city, postcode, country, phone, email, website, description and category, and choose the status (pending by default). The address is found on the map when the entry is sent; if it can’t be found, the location is marked “Address not found” and stays unpublished for you to check. A logged-in submitter becomes the location’s author and sees it under “My locations” (<code>[matrixmap_my_locations]</code>). Forms may create up to 100 locations an hour (<code>matrixmap_pro_forms_hourly_limit</code>); entries past that are kept by the form plugin but not turned into locations."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:531
msgid "<strong>WPForms</strong>: form builder → Settings → MatrixMap. An Address field mapped to “Street address” also fills city, state, postcode and country."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:532
msgid "<strong>Fluent Forms</strong>: form → Settings & Integrations → Integrations → Add new → MatrixMap location. Conditional logic decides when a location is created."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:533
msgid "<strong>Gravity Forms</strong>: form → Settings → MatrixMap → Add new feed, with the usual feed conditions."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:534
msgid "<strong>Defaults</strong>: Settings → Forms sets the default status, a category for every form location and who is notified."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:536
msgid "Nothing loads unless the builder or form plugin is active: without it there is no extra code and no settings to see."
msgstr ""

